// D1690's three-member axis, and its OTHER outcome: where the two-member template's capture
// prints a wrong value, a three-member one whose sets differ in a REF member traps at run
// time instead. Same mechanism, same ingredient — a declared row nothing constructs — so the
// two templates must move together.
//
// The value boxes `i32 | boolean | string` and holds the i32 `7`; `type H`'s box is
// `string | boolean | i64`, and reading the payload at the wrong tag is a cast failure rather
// than a mis-read scalar. Graded by PRINTED VALUE, like its two-member sibling.
//
// `type H` is never named by a value; declaring it is the whole ingredient.
//
// Two spellings measured NOT to be defects, and deliberately not templates: the same three
// members in a different ORDER (the two unions coincide), and a two-member value against a
// three-member row that contains it (the tags align). The widening control — the same pair
// DELIVERED to the wider row — lives in
// `tests/cases/structs/anon-struct-declared-box-row-not-captured.vl`.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type U3 = i32 | boolean | string
type U5 = string | boolean | i64
type H = { xs: U5 }
function u3(): U3 { return 7 }
function u3b(): U3 { return 8 }
// @@VALUE@@
{ xs: u3() }
// @@TYPE@@
{ xs: U3 }
// @@PROOF@@
print(v.xs)
// @@WANT@@
7
// @@VALUE2@@
{ xs: u3b() }
// @@TYPE2@@
{ xs: U3 }
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v.xs)
// @@WANT2@@
8
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a struct, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
